  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The breakout is drawn plugged into the top half of the breadboard (rows f-j in the image), columns 4-9. This is mapped to catalogue bank 'b' (rows f-j), with the breakout pins in row j and the jumper wires in row i of the same columns.",
   "Pin mapping follows the tutorial table: A0=Self-test, A1=Z, A2=Y, A3=X, A4=GND (driven LOW in code), A5=VDD (driven HIGH in code). The schematic's X/Z crossing is drawn differently, but the table and code are used.",
   "The accelerometer is powered from analog pins A4/A5 used as digital outputs, not from the 5V and GND pins. The tutorial warns that some boards are 3.3V only.",
   "The catalogue type adxl335 stands in for the generic ADXL3xx breakout."
  ]
 },
